The sequence must be sorted under the comparison being used. Without sortedness, the invariant that each step can safely discard half the remaining interval collapses — the midpoint comparison no longer tells you which half to search, so correctness is lost entirely.

The half-open interval `[l, r)` is the canonical way to maintain that invariant: it keeps the narrowest possible range and makes the `l = mid + 1` / `r = mid` updates uniform and consistent across iterations.

