A **valid** argument is one where, if the premises were true, the conclusion would necessarily follow — the truth of the premises guarantees the truth of the conclusion. A **sound** argument goes further: it is valid *and* its premises are actually true in the real world. Validity is about logical structure alone; soundness adds factual correctness.
</answer>

